From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@t1100.local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:51:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: drop the own ramoops region

LK reserves 0x70000000-0x7000ffff as ibc-reserved. Any /reserved-memory
child overlapping a LK reservation makes it print
"reserved_memory_conflict_check fatal error keep while (1)" and reset
before jumping to the kernel, which is exactly what happened to every
image carrying ramoops@70000000.

pstore now uses the vendor window LK reserves and exports through the
kernel command line (ramoops.mem_address=0x54410000, mem_size=0xe0000),
registered by fs/pstore/ram.c from the cmdline parameters.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts  | 29 +++++++------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index 3c8e04481..029ff4264 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -790,22 +790,15 @@ &dsi_out {
 #include "mt6771-fplus-t1100-lk-compat.dtsi"
 
 /*
- * Own pstore/ramoops region. LK reserves its ram_console/ramoops blocks as
- * `nomap`, and mainline ramoops cannot memremap() a nomap region, so
- * /sys/fs/pstore stays empty. This 1 MiB block sits inside System RAM, does
- * not overlap any LK reservation (checked by check-lk-dtb.py) and is not
- * nomap, so pstore works and survives a warm reboot.
+ * No own ramoops node on purpose.
+ *
+ * LK on this board reserves 0x70000000-0x7000ffff as "ibc-reserved" and, on
+ * any /reserved-memory child that overlaps one of its own reservations, prints
+ * "reserved_memory_conflict_check fatal error keep while (1)" and resets the
+ * board before jumping to the kernel. The previous 1 MiB ramoops@70000000 hit
+ * exactly that.
+ *
+ * pstore therefore uses the vendor window LK reserves for us and puts into the
+ * kernel command line (ramoops.mem_address=0x54410000, mem_size=0xe0000),
+ * which fs/pstore/ram.c registers from the cmdline parameters.
  */
-&{/reserved-memory} {
-	#address-cells = <2>;
-	#size-cells = <2>;
-	ranges;
-
-	ramoops@70000000 {
-		compatible = "ramoops";
-		reg = <0 0x70000000 0 0x100000>;
-		record-size  = <0x20000>;
-		console-size = <0x80000>;
-		pmsg-size    = <0x20000>;
-	};
-};
